    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75997" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρίᾰχος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], ὁ, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρά</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bottom</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγχεος οὐ</span>. <i>butt-end</i>
			of the spear, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.443
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1253
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.111
			</span></i> (Antip.), <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				9.15
			</span></i>; of an arrow-head, the part fixed in the shaft,
			<i>tang</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.88
			</span></i> (v. l.); apptly. <i>stem</i> of a candlestick in <i><span class="en">
				Call.
			</span></i><i>Fr.anon.</i><i><span class="en">
				50
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>part of an oar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.90
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρακός</span>
			).</div>
